63
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,420
When the ball appeared to come in contact with the paddle,

64
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:42,420
an electronic signal was sent to a logic circuit that triggered

65
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:47,420
an output signal to a so-called flip-flop switch.

66
00:03:47,421 --> 00:03:50,460
The signal caused the flip-flop to alter its state and change

67
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:53,120
the direction of the ball.

68
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:55,900
This phenomenon occurred every time the ball touched a paddle

69
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:56,800
or a wall.

70
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,960
Although groundbreaking, Bears' ping-pong

71
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:05,740
lacked some fundamental gaming elements, such as sound

72
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:06,900
and a score counter.

73
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:07,840
Missed it.

74
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:09,940
One up.

75
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:10,940
Keep it on the...

