128
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:50,980
eight directional joystick with a single red button, the

129
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:54,300
revolutionary console produced an offspring of the Mi decade

130
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:58,800
known as the gamer. A multi-billion dollar industry

131
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:00,800
was off and running.

132
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:12,940
The key component that made the Atari 2600 sing

133
00:07:12,941 --> 00:07:16,940
was a tiny high-tech wonder born in the 70s destined to transform

134
00:07:16,941 --> 00:07:24,940
technology, the microprocessor, or simply the chip.

135
00:07:24,941 --> 00:07:28,940
The electronic ancestor to the chip was the bulky vacuum tube.

136
00:07:28,941 --> 00:07:32,940
It was replaced by the smaller transistor in the 1960s.

137
00:07:32,941 --> 00:07:36,940
By the 1970s, engineers were building transistors of

138
00:07:36,941 --> 00:07:40,940
microscopic size. A transistor can turn the flow of a

139
00:07:40,941 --> 00:07:44,940
current on or off, allowing it to process the binary language

140
00:07:44,941 --> 00:07:48,940
of a computer. By placing thousands of transistors

141
00:07:48,941 --> 00:07:52,940
onto a semiconductor, engineers generated the processing power

142
00:07:52,941 --> 00:07:56,940
of a large computer on a single chip.

143
00:07:56,941 --> 00:08:02,940
In 1971, Intel engineered the world's first microprocessor.

144
00:08:02,941 --> 00:08:06,680
and designated it the Intel 4004.

145
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:10,040
It was the first computer on a chip.

146
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:14,140
In fact, when we advertised it, and that was November of 1971,

147
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:16,960
it was not a modest ad.

148
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:20,340
We said announcing a new era of integrated electronics.

149
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:24,180
As chip integration got big,

150
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:27,360
the size of electronics started getting small.

151
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:30,740
One of the first new gadgets produced by this giant leap

152
00:08:30,741 --> 00:08:36,340
towards miniaturization was the pocket calculator.

153
00:08:36,341 --> 00:08:42,180
Leading the way in 1972 was Hewlett Packard's HP 35.

154
00:08:42,181 --> 00:08:46,220
Its $395 price tag may have been a few too many numbers

155
00:08:46,221 --> 00:08:48,460
