00:29:25,701 --> 00:29:31,620
Mr. Coffee, the original automatic drip coffee maker.

515
00:29:31,621 --> 00:29:35,620
Since its debut in 1972, Mr. Coffee has been the world's

516
00:29:35,621 --> 00:29:39,360
number one coffee maker, selling over 50 million units.

517
00:29:41,860 --> 00:29:45,860
Before Mr. Coffee, Java junkies relied on percolators.

518
00:29:45,960 --> 00:29:48,500
They worked well enough, but their method of operation

519
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:53,000
was to boil the coffee grounds, which created a bitter brew.

520
00:29:53,100 --> 00:29:58,100
So what's the method behind Mr. Coffee's refined brewing prowess?

521
00:29:58,200 --> 00:30:01,520
Let's brew a pot and find out.

522
00:30:01,620 --> 00:30:03,820
We poured the water into the water tank.

523
00:30:03,920 --> 00:30:05,320
That's this assembly.

524
00:30:05,420 --> 00:30:08,060
It's got a heat-activated valve on the bottom,

525
00:30:08,160 --> 00:30:10,760
and that valve responds to the heat generated

526
00:30:10,761 --> 00:30:14,060
generated by this coil on the inside of this heater.

527
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:16,260
As that heats up, it opens up the valve

528
00:30:16,360 --> 00:30:17,960
and lets water into the coil.

529
00:30:18,060 --> 00:30:20,800
And that water flows out through the middle,

530
00:30:20,900 --> 00:30:22,500
above the brew basket.

531
00:30:22,600 --> 00:30:25,400
And the result of all of this is coffee that

532
00:30:25,500 --> 00:30:28,620
is made at the proper time and temperature

533
00:30:28,720 --> 00:30:31,820
for the best extraction possible.

534
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:34,820
When Mr. Coffee was released in 1972,

535
00:30:34,920 --> 00:30:39,020
it quickly became America's number one coffee maker.

536
00:30:39,021 --> 00:30:42,520
35 years later, he's had a few facelifts,

537
00:30:42,620 --> 00:30:44,320
but he still brews a mean cup of joe.

538
00:30:47,320 --> 00:30:49,900
Mr. Coffee wasn't the only new appliance in the 70s

539
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:52,960
