540
00:30:53,060 --> 00:30:56,500
By 1970, the microwave oven started nuking meals in a

541
00:30:56,600 --> 00:31:00,940
fraction of the time required by conventional ovens.

542
00:31:01,040 --> 00:31:05,340
The secret to its cooking efficiency is the magnetron.

543
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:07,320
The magnetron, which is essentially

544
00:31:07,321 --> 00:31:12,660
an X-ray emitting source which is steered through electromagnets.

545
00:31:12,760 --> 00:31:17,560
What it does is very precisely put out a spray of microwaves

546
00:31:17,660 --> 00:31:22,960
and cooks by jiggling the water molecules in your food.

547
00:31:23,060 --> 00:31:24,560
The invention of the microwave oven

548
00:31:24,660 --> 00:31:27,280
stems from the Raytheon company's work in building

549
00:31:27,380 --> 00:31:30,280
radar magnetrons during World War II.

550
00:31:30,380 --> 00:31:34,920
The magnetron was developed to increase the ability of World

551
00:31:34,921 --> 00:31:38,260
to detect airplanes, create a smaller frequency

552
00:31:38,360 --> 00:31:40,660
of wavelength, which is called the microwave.

553
00:31:40,760 --> 00:31:43,060
Towards the end of the war, the Raytheon company,

554
00:31:43,160 --> 00:31:45,660
which was the major manufacturer of magnetrons

555
00:31:45,760 --> 00:31:47,560
for the military, they needed to come up

556
00:31:47,660 --> 00:31:50,660
with some other use for the magnetrons that they had.

557
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:52,300
So what they thought was, well, let's

558
00:31:52,400 --> 00:31:53,800
see if we can use them for cooking.

559
00:31:53,900 --> 00:31:56,180
Let's see if we can develop an oven for them.

560
00:31:56,280 --> 00:32:00,680
In 1954, Raytheon produced the first commercial microwave

561
00:32:00,780 --> 00:32:02,320
oven.

